    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269-a5">

                <pb facs="0364" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg290"/>

                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Marseilles</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 26, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Senator:</hi> I have the honor to annex under
                    this enclosure copy of a pamphlet which has been sent to me from Washington to
                    be distributed in localities dependent on my consulate, as well as some lines in
                    explanation, which I propose to have printed and to add the thereto, in
                    conformity with the wishes of my government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, Mr. Senator, to submit these documents to your appreciation,
                    and to request you will please to let me know, if any objections exist, or what
                    will be the formalities necessary to permit the distribution.</p>
                <p>Please accept, sir and senator, the assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE W. VAN HORNE, <hi rendition="#italic">Consul of the United
                            States.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Senator</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Charged
                            with the Administration of the Department of the Bouches du
                        Rhone.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
